    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103908" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῐθαιβώσσω</span></b> , of bees, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>store up honey</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				13.106
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>store up, put away</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνδοθι γωρυτοῖο τιθαιβώσσουσα κάλυψε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antim.
				</span></i>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMilan.</u>
				17.37
			</span></i> (glossed <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιθεῖσα καὶ
				ἀποθησαυρίζουσα</span> ibid.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>supply with food, foster, cherish</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέκνα τ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				199
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γύας τ. ἀρδηθμῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					622
				</span></i>
			.</div>
